---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import profileImage from "../assets/images/joe_laskowski.webp";
import locationImage from "../assets/images/south-bend.webp";

// Career start: 2000. Total years in IT is computed at build time
// so the About page stays current without manual edits each year.
const CAREER_START_YEAR = 2000;
const LINUX_START_YEAR = 2007;
const yearsInIT = new Date().getFullYear() - CAREER_START_YEAR;
const linuxYears = new Date().getFullYear() - LINUX_START_YEAR;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About Me | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description={`Joe Laskowski — ${yearsInIT} years in IT, currently working in AI, writing here when I've got something worth saying.`}
>
  <div class="container">
    <article class="about-content">
      <div class="hero-section">
        <Image
          src={profileImage}
          alt="Joe Laskowski"
          class="profile-image"
          width={180}
          height={180}
          loading="eager"
        />
        <div class="hero-text">
          <h1 class="gradient-text">About Joe Laskowski</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Started in 2000 running the box-mover crew on a Whirlpool
            deployment. {yearsInIT} years later I'm AI Quality Analyst at
            Aunalytics — a title I would have laughed at five years ago
            and now do every day. This is where I write when what I'm
            building wants to be a sentence instead of a commit message.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2 class="accent-blue">The Work</h2>
        <p>
          By week two I'd been pulled into the deployment work alongside
          the techs and was quietly running circles around them. That
          three-month project stretched to a year. Then years of on-site
          warranty work for HP, Dell, Sony, and the rest of the OEMs. Then close to a decade managing field techs across
          the country from my basement. Then nine years at Aunalytics —
          service desk, service desk lead, Internal IT — the last
          stretch spent living in Microsoft 365, Active Directory, Intune,
          and Entra/Azure (which Microsoft has renamed enough times that
          I've stopped keeping count out of self-respect). Long enough,
          either way, to have watched the same "new" framework get
          rebranded twice and sold back to me. Long enough to have strong
          opinions about why the PowerShell window went red at 2 AM.
        </p>

        <p>
          In April 2026 the role shifted to AI Quality Analyst at <a
            href="https://www.aunalytics.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aunalytics</a
          > — the Midwest data platform company that's been the day job
          for the last nine of those years. Stripped of the title, the
          work comes down to this: when the AI says something, is it
          actually right? Turns out that's a more interesting question
          than the marketing for any of these systems would have you
          believe.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-green">Building</h2>
        <p>
          Outside the day job there's <a href="https://autoscript.studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >AutoScript Studio LLC</a
          > — my Indiana company, and the legal wrapper around the things
          I'm slowly shipping. The brand under it is
          <strong>PixelDrops</strong>, an AI-driven digital-products
          operation: a novel I wrote under a pen name (Amazon launch
          coming), a YouTube channel called <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/@StackTraceDocs"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">StackTraceDocs</a
          > (first video out, production pipeline in iteration before the
          next one), and whatever software ships out of the workshop after
          that. Everything leans hard on AI tooling
          — that's the whole point of doing it now. The blog is where the
          first version of any of it tends to surface.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-purple">Off the Clock</h2>
        <p>
          Linux every day for {linuxYears} years — the terminal is where
          I think clearest. Been an XRP obsessive since 2017 — full
          conviction, no exit plan, XRP Army 4 Life. Sold my $XLM bag a
          while back to buy more XRP because the math kept making sense
          (and still does). Ask me about it if you want to lose an hour
          of your day. The rest of my screen-time goes to AI tooling
          (anything new I can poke at, I poke at), the biohacking side
          of health and longevity, and the UAP disclosure rabbit hole.
          Most of what falls out ends up on the blog. The rest ends up
          in a drawer.
        </p>

        <p>
          Away from the screen: IPAs of every persuasion (I shop by ABV;
          the higher, the better), hot wings ordered at a heat level my
          friends consider a personal failing, miles on the Mishawaka
          Riverwalk (my home away from home), and I'm Star Wars enough
          to keep watching but not enough to fight about it.
        </p>

        <div class="image-section">
          <Image
            src={locationImage}
            alt="South Bend, Indiana"
            class="location-image"
            width={600}
            height={400}
            loading="eager"
          />
          <p class="image-caption">South Bend, Indiana</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="accent-orange">Family</h2>
        <p>
          Three kids and four grandkids — my two oldest are grown and out
          doing their own thing; AJ, my youngest, is still a kid, with me
          several days a week. The grandkids are sharper than I
          was at their age and significantly louder. My partner Rianna and
          I started dating on New Year's Day 2025, and between her three
          kids and mine the house is rarely quiet — which, most days, is
          the point.
        </p>

        <p>
          South Bend, Indiana. Real place. Notre Dame, the river, winters
          that make the terminal feel like a coping mechanism. I grew up
          here, my kids did too, and I'm not going anywhere.
        </p>

        <p>
          Under all of it: a foundation under the people I love, a future
          with Rianna that doesn't depend on which of the side bets pays
          off. The day job covers the floor. The rest is the ceiling I'm
          trying to raise.
        </p>

        <h2 class="accent-pink">Let's Connect</h2>
        <p>
          If you want to talk XRP, AI tooling, or whether the UAP stuff
          is finally about to break wide open — social links are in the
          header. The <a href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">blog</a>
          is whatever I've been chewing on lately. Or <a href="/contact/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >send me a message</a
          > and we'll go from there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <style>
    .about-content {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hero-section {
      display: flex;
      gap: 3rem;
      align-items: center;
      margin: 3rem 0;
      padding: 2rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    }

    .profile-image {
      width: 180px;
      height: 180px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      border: 4px solid var(--accent-blue);
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.2);
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .hero-text {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .hero-text h1 {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .prose {
      margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .prose h2 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .prose p {
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .prose a {
      color: var(--accent-blue);
      font-weight: 600;
      transition:
        color 0.2s ease,
        text-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }

    .prose a:hover {
      color: var(--accent-cyan);
      text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.3);
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .image-section {
      margin: 3rem 0;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .location-image {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 600px;
      height: auto;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
      margin: 0 auto 1rem auto;
      display: block;
    }

    .image-caption {
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .hero-section {
        flex-direction: column;
        text-align: center;
        gap: 2rem;
      }

      .hero-text h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .lead {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
      }

      .profile-image {
        width: 150px;
        height: 150px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
